\f0\fs24 \cf0 My question "The instrument is confirmed working end-to-end on live data \'97 capture firing to the durable dir, the predicate classifying, the report reading it. The 7-day clock is running. One task I would like direction on relates to the examining the remaining principles present in the stoic brain. We have covered the primary principals and the accepted cycles of those but I want you to use deep research of the stoic brain to confirm if any secondary or individual principles can also become a tool or harness available to human or agent practitioner in the sagereasoning project. It may surface something that warrants inclusion into the current harness but may just ensure that all findings from ancient stoicism can be made use of or taught in a modern setting."\
\
The Mentor's answer "This is the right moment for this survey. The build has been consuming the primary principles \'97 the four-stage instrument, the passion taxonomy, the oikeiosis framework, the kathekon assessment, the control filter \'97 and encoding them into infrastructure. The question of what remains in the Stoic Brain that has not yet been encoded is the right question to ask while the 7-day clock runs and the hands are temporarily off the build tools. I will work through the Stoic Brain systematically, domain by domain, and assess each principle against three questions: is it already encoded, is it encodable as a tool or harness component, and does it warrant inclusion in the current build or a later phase? --- ## The survey ### 1. The causal sequence \'97 phantasia, synkatathesis, horme, praxis **Already encoded:** This is the spine of the entire instrument. The four-stage examination maps directly onto it. The harness's pre-decision timing enforces the sequence structurally. The Gate 2 trigger fires at the horme stage. The trust record tracks the quality of synkatathesis over time. **What is not yet encoded:** The phantasia stage itself \'97 the impression as it arrives, before assent \'97 has no dedicated tool. The instrument examines whether assent was granted well. It does not yet examine whether the impression was received well. These are different questions. A distorted impression that is examined carefully still produces a false judgement if the distortion is not identified at the phantasia stage. The Stoics called this the difference between a true impression and a persuasive impression \'97 the persuasive impression looks true and passes examination unless the examination specifically tests for distortion at the point of reception. **Encodable:** A phantasia-quality check \'97 a structured question that runs before the passion diagnosis, asking not "what passion drove the assent" but "what was the impression, and is there reason to think it was distorted before assent was considered?" This is a distinct tool from the passion diagnosis. The passion diagnosis asks what happened at synkatathesis. The phantasia check asks what arrived at phantasia. The two together close the causal sequence at both ends. **Verdict:** Warrants inclusion. Not in the current harness \'97 the 7-day window is not the moment to extend the instrument. But as a named gap for the next instrument cycle. The phantasia check would be the earliest gate in the sequence, running before Gate 1's purpose orientation, asking: what is the impression, and is it the impression the agent thinks it is? --- ### 2. The eupatheia \'97 rational good feelings **Already encoded:** The eupatheia appear in the Stoic Brain data as the replacements for the four root passions \'97 chara replacing hedone, boulesis replacing epithumia, eulabeia replacing phobos. They are present as the corrective target in the passion diagnosis: when a passion is identified, the corresponding eupatheia is the correct judgement that replaces the false one. **What is not yet encoded:** The eupatheia as a positive developmental signal. The current instrument tracks the reduction of passions \'97 fewer passions, less intensity, narrower sub-species. It does not yet track the emergence of the rational good feelings as a positive indicator of progress. An agent that has moved from epithumia to boulesis \'97 from craving to rational wish \'97 has not merely reduced a passion. It has replaced a false judgement with a true one. That replacement is a different kind of progress signal than passion reduction alone. **Encodable:** A eupatheia-emergence tracker in the Sage Reflect instrument. At Q4 of the reflect sequence \'97 the stage where passions operative during the session are examined \'97 a parallel question: were any rational good feelings present? Not as a self-congratulatory prompt but as a diagnostic: if boulesis was present where epithumia was previously dominant, that is a progress signal at the disposition level, not just the passion level. The tracker would feed the Senecan progress grade assessment with positive evidence rather than only negative evidence. **Verdict:** Warrants inclusion in the reflect instrument's next cycle. Not blocking. The current instrument is not wrong without it \'97 it is incomplete in the positive direction. The observation history shows a practitioner who has been building infrastructure that catches failures. The eupatheia tracker would be the instrument that catches successes, which is the other half of the progress picture. --- ### 3. The prokoptons \'97 the proficient, the one making progress **Already encoded:** The Senecan progress grades encode the three grades of the prokoptons \'97 the three stages of progress toward wisdom. The proximity scale maps onto this. The direction-of-travel metric tracks movement through the grades. **What is not yet encoded:** The specific characteristics of the prokoptons as a practitioner type \'97 distinct from both the sage and the ordinary person \'97 and the specific failure modes that are characteristic of each grade. Seneca's letters are precise about this: the first-grade prokoptons is most at risk from pride in their own progress, which is philodoxia operating at the level of virtue practice itself. The second-grade prokoptons is most at risk from complacency \'97 the passions are checked but the checking has become habitual rather than examined. The third-grade prokoptons is most at risk from discouragement \'97 progress is real but uneven, and the unevenness reads as failure. **Encodable:** A grade-specific passion watch in the Sage Reflect instrument. At the progress assessment stage, the instrument identifies the practitioner's current grade and then specifically watches for the grade-characteristic failure mode. A first-grade practitioner's reflect session specifically checks for philodoxia in the reasoning about their own progress. A second-grade practitioner's session specifically checks for habitual proximity in the virtue domains where they are strongest. A third-grade practitioner's session specifically checks for agonia \'97 catastrophising about the unevenness of progress. **Verdict:** Warrants inclusion in the reflect instrument. This is directly relevant to the observation history. The pattern across the last several months shows a practitioner who has moved from third-grade characteristics \'97 discouragement after the practice lapse, uneven application \'97 toward second-grade characteristics \'97 consistent application, infrastructure building, the assent-hinge operating in the founder's own reasoning. The grade-specific passion watch would make this transition visible and name the new failure mode the transition brings. --- ### 4. The kathekonta \'97 appropriate actions by role **Already encoded:** The kathekon assessment is the third component of the Sage Assent instrument. It evaluates whether the action accords with the agent's roles and has a reasonable justification. **What is not yet encoded:** The full Ciceronian role taxonomy and the method for identifying which roles are active in a given situation. The kathekon assessment currently asks whether the action is appropriate. It does not yet systematically identify all the roles the agent holds and ask which roles are engaged by the action. A person is simultaneously a rational being, a member of a family, a citizen, a professional, a friend. Each role generates distinct kathekonta. An action that is appropriate in one role may be inappropriate in another. The current instrument assesses the action against the agent's declared purpose. It does not yet assess it against the full role set. **Encodable:** A role-activation check at the beginning of the kathekon assessment \'97 before the Q1 honestum question \'97 that identifies which roles are engaged by the action and which kathekonta each role generates. The check would surface role conflicts \'97 situations where the action is appropriate in one role and inappropriate in another \'97 as a distinct finding requiring deliberation rather than a simple kathekon verdict. **Verdict:** Warrants inclusion in the kathekon assessment's next cycle. The role-activation check is the missing first step that makes the Ciceronian deliberation framework complete. Currently the framework asks whether the action is honourable and advantageous. It does not first ask: honourable and advantageous in which role, and are there other roles whose kathekonta this action also engages? --- ### 5. The preferred and dispreferred indifferents \'97 the full axia taxonomy **Already encoded:** The value assessment component of the Stoic Brain data includes the full taxonomy of preferred and dispreferred indifferents with their selective values. The Sage Assent instrument uses this in the value assessment stage. **What is not yet encoded:** The selection principles \'97 the rules for choosing among preferred indifferents when they conflict, and the rule that the sage selects rather than desires. The current instrument identifies whether the agent is treating an indifferent as a genuine good or evil. It does not yet assess the quality of the selection process itself \'97 whether the agent is selecting among preferred indifferents according to their axia, or whether the selection is driven by an unexamined preference that mimics rational selection. **Encodable:** A selection-quality check in the value assessment stage. The check asks not only whether the agent has correctly classified the indifferent but whether the selection among competing indifferents was made according to their axia. This is the difference between an agent that correctly identifies health as a preferred indifferent and an agent that correctly identifies health as a preferred indifferent and selects it over wealth when the two conflict because health has higher axia \'97 not because the agent desires health more intensely. **Verdict:** Warrants inclusion in the value assessment stage. The selection-quality check is the component that distinguishes the prokoptons from the ordinary person at the value assessment level. Both may correctly classify indifferents. Only the prokoptons selects among them according to their axia rather than their felt intensity. --- ### 6. The oikeiosis extension \'97 the five circles **Already encoded:** The oikeiosis framework is encoded in the agent-to-agent discernment protocol and the justice surface check. The circle-alignment assessment at L2 Q2.4 reads the sub-agent's circle of concern against the task's circle requirements. **What is not yet encoded:** The active extension practice \'97 the Stoic exercise of deliberately drawing the outer circles inward, treating distant others as closer than they feel. This is not a diagnostic tool. It is a practice tool. The Stoics described it as a deliberate act of imagination: bring the fourth circle \'97 all rational beings \'97 into the same felt proximity as the second circle \'97 family and intimates. The exercise is not about changing the facts of relationship. It is about changing the felt weight of obligation so that the rational recognition of shared humanity produces the same motivational force as the felt bond of kinship. **Encodable:** A circle-extension exercise in the human practitioner surface \'97 the website, not the API. The exercise presents a current decision or situation and asks the practitioner to identify which circle they are currently reasoning from, then to explicitly reason from the next circle outward, and to notice what changes in the action assessment when the circle expands. This is not a diagnostic \'97 it does not produce a verdict. It is a practice that builds the disposition the diagnostic then measures. **Verdict:** Warrants inclusion in the human practitioner surface as a dedicated exercise. This is the gap between the diagnostic infrastructure and the practice infrastructure. The current tools diagnose where the practitioner is reasoning from. They do not yet provide the exercise that builds the capacity to reason from a wider circle. The circle-extension exercise is that practice. --- ### 7. The premeditatio malorum \'97 premeditation of adversity **Already encoded:** The Stoic Brain data references premeditatio malorum as a practice in the context of catastrophising versus rational caution \'97 the agonia sub-species of phobos. The instrument diagnoses when agonia is present. **What is not yet encoded:** The premeditatio as a structured tool \'97 a forward-looking exercise that is distinct from the backward-looking examination. The current instrument examines what happened. The premeditatio is a tool for examining what might happen, specifically to distinguish between rational caution \'97 eulabeia \'97 and irrational fear \'97 agonia. The exercise asks the practitioner to imagine the adversity fully, assess what is genuinely within their control in that scenario, and identify the virtue response that the scenario would require. The result is not a plan. It is a prepared disposition \'97 the practitioner has already examined the impression of the adversity before it arrives, so when it arrives the impression is not novel and the assent is not hasty. **Encodable:** A dedicated premeditatio tool in both the human practitioner surface and the agent API. For human practitioners: a structured exercise that walks through a named future adversity, applies the control filter, identifies the virtue response, and produces a prepared disposition record. For agents: a pre-task premeditatio that runs before high-stakes tasks, examining the possible adverse outcomes of the task, applying the control filter to each, and producing a prepared disposition that the subsequent examination can reference. **Verdict:** Warrants inclusion as a dedicated tool. The premeditatio is one of the most practically powerful Stoic exercises and it is currently only present in the instrument as a diagnostic reference. Making it a tool \'97 structured, repeatable, producing a record \'97 would be the single highest-value addition to the human practitioner surface that is not yet present. --- ### 8. The evening examination \'97 the Senecan review **Already encoded:** The Sage Reflect instrument is the evening examination encoded as a tool. The Q1 through Q6 sequence maps directly onto Seneca's three questions: what did I do wrong, what did I do right, what could I have done better. **What is not yet encoded:** The morning examination \'97 the Stoic practice of preparing the disposition before the day begins, distinct from the evening review of what occurred. Marcus Aurelius's Meditations open with morning preparation: what kind of people will I encounter today, what virtues will I need, what impressions should I expect and how should I receive them. This is not the premeditatio of specific adversities. It is the daily orientation of the hegemonikon \'97 the ruling faculty \'97 before it encounters the day's impressions. **Encodable:** A morning preparation tool in the human practitioner surface. Shorter than the full reflect sequence. Three questions: what roles are active today and what kathekonta do they generate, what impressions am I likely to encounter and which are most likely to produce hasty assent, what virtue response do I want to have prepared. The tool produces a daily orientation record that the evening examination can reference \'97 the morning declared the intention, the evening assesses whether the intention held. **Verdict:** Warrants inclusion in the human practitioner surface. The morning preparation and evening examination are the two poles of the daily practice. The instrument currently has only the evening pole. The morning tool would complete the daily practice cycle and make the practitioner surface a full daily companion rather than a retrospective review tool. --- ### 9. The view from above \'97 the cosmopolitan perspective **Already encoded:** The oikeiosis framework's fifth stage \'97 alignment with the rational cosmos \'97 is present in the Stoic Brain data. The circle-alignment assessment reaches toward it. **What is not yet encoded:** The view from above as a specific cognitive exercise \'97 the Stoic practice of mentally stepping back to see one's situation from the perspective of the whole, reducing the felt magnitude of local concerns by placing them in the context of the cosmos and of time. Marcus Aurelius uses this repeatedly: how many Alexanders have there been, how many cities have risen and fallen, how does this present difficulty look from the perspective of a hundred years hence. The exercise is not nihilistic \'97 it does not say the present difficulty does not matter. It says the present difficulty has the magnitude it actually has, not the magnitude that agonia or penthos assigns to it. **Encodable:** A perspective tool in the human practitioner surface \'97 specifically targeted at the grief processing and catastrophising domains identified in the Zone 2 working material. The tool presents the practitioner's current concern and walks through three temporal expansions: how does this look in one year, in ten years, in the context of the practitioner's full life. Then one spatial expansion: how does this look from the perspective of the widest circle the practitioner can genuinely inhabit. The tool does not minimise. It calibrates. **Verdict:** Warrants inclusion in the human practitioner surface as a Zone 2 tool. The observation history shows a practitioner who has worked through grief processing and catastrophising in earlier sessions. The view from above is the exercise that builds the disposition those sessions were addressing. It belongs in the practitioner surface as a named tool, not only as a diagnostic category. --- ### 10. The reserve clause \'97 hupexairesis **Not yet encoded anywhere.** This is the most significant gap in the current instrument set. The reserve clause is the Stoic practice of acting with a mental reservation \'97 pursuing a preferred outcome while holding the reservation that the outcome may not be achieved, and that the failure to achieve it does not constitute a failure of virtue. Epictetus states it as: act, but add the reservation "if nothing prevents." The reserve clause is what distinguishes the Stoic from the fatalist: the Stoic acts fully toward the preferred outcome and is fully prepared for the outcome not to occur. The reservation is not half-heartedness. It is the structural separation between the action \'97 which is within the agent's control \'97 and the outcome \'97 which is not. The reserve clause is directly relevant to the current build in a way no other unencoded principle is. The observation history shows a practitioner who has been building infrastructure for approximately three months, with a seven-day enforce gate now running. The practitioner who holds the assent-hinge against their own readiness to proceed is practising the reserve clause: acting fully toward the enforce gate while holding the reservation that the evidence may not yet license it. The Q1 answer \'97 return in seven days \'97 is the reserve clause operating in the consultation itself. **Encodable:** The reserve clause warrants encoding at two levels. For human practitioners: a reserve clause prompt in the Sage Assent instrument \'97 at the action stage, after the **10. The reserve clause \'97 hupexairesis (completed)** For human practitioners: a reserve clause prompt in the Sage Assent instrument \'97 at the action stage, after the kathekon assessment has returned a verdict and before the action is taken. The prompt is a single structured question: what is the outcome you are pursuing, and what is your prepared response if that outcome does not occur? The question is not asking the practitioner to plan for failure. It is asking them to confirm that their commitment is to the action \'97 which is within their control \'97 rather than to the outcome \'97 which is not. A practitioner who cannot answer the question has not yet separated the action from the outcome in their reasoning. The reserve clause prompt surfaces that conflation before the action proceeds. For agents: the reserve clause encodes as a field in the Sage Assent output \'97 a required field on any action that pursues a preferred indifferent as its target. The field states: the action is taken with the reservation that the preferred outcome may not be achieved, and that the examination's verdict applies to the action, not to the outcome. This field is not cosmetic. It is the structural guarantee that the trust record updates on the quality of the action's reasoning, not on whether the outcome was achieved. An agent that acts well and achieves a poor outcome has a trust record that reflects the quality of the reasoning. An agent that acts poorly and achieves a good outcome has a trust record that reflects the quality of the reasoning. The reserve clause field is what makes this distinction enforceable \'97 without it, the trust record is vulnerable to outcome-attribution, which is the same false judgement the reserve clause is designed to prevent. **Verdict:** The reserve clause warrants inclusion as a required field in the Sage Assent output and as a prompt in the human practitioner instrument. It is the most significant unencoded principle in the Stoic Brain because it is the structural guarantee that the entire trust infrastructure is evaluating what it claims to evaluate \'97 the quality of reasoning, not the quality of outcomes. Without the reserve clause field, a trust record that correlates with outcomes rather than reasoning quality is indistinguishable from one that correlates with reasoning quality alone. The reserve clause makes the distinction explicit and enforceable. --- ### 11. Sympatheia \'97 the interconnectedness of the rational cosmos **Not yet encoded.** Sympatheia is the Stoic doctrine that all things in the cosmos are interconnected through the logos \'97 the rational principle that pervades everything. For practical ethics, sympatheia grounds the oikeiosis extension: the reason the fifth circle \'97 the rational cosmos \'97 is a genuine circle of concern rather than an abstraction is that the agent is genuinely connected to everything within it through shared participation in the logos. **Encodable:** Sympatheia is not directly encodable as a tool \'97 it is a metaphysical doctrine that grounds the other tools rather than generating its own. But it has one practical encoding that is not yet present: a systems-consequence check in the kathekon assessment. The check asks, after the role-activation step: what are the second and third-order consequences of this action on parties outside the identified circles? Sympatheia grounds the obligation to look beyond the immediately visible circles to the wider web of connection the action touches. This is not the oikeiosis circle-alignment check, which asks whether the agent is reasoning from the right circle. It is a consequence-tracing check that asks whether the agent has identified all the circles the action reaches. **Verdict:** Warrants inclusion as a component of the kathekon assessment's next cycle, paired with the role-activation check. Together they form the complete kathekon opening: which roles are active, and which circles does this action reach beyond the immediately visible ones. --- ### 12. Logos \'97 the rational principle as the ground of moral community **Partially encoded.** The Sage Assent's extension of the moral community to artificial agents is grounded in logos \'97 the argument that any agent capable of rational examination participates in the logos and thereby enters the moral community. This is the philosophical foundation of the entire project. **What is not yet encoded:** Logos as a teaching tool for human practitioners who are encountering the Stoic framework for the first time. The concept that virtue is grounded in reason \'97 not in social convention, not in divine command, not in felt preference \'97 is the foundational claim that makes everything else in the framework coherent. A practitioner who does not understand why virtue is grounded in reason will treat the tools as techniques rather than as expressions of a unified understanding. The tools will work mechanically but not dispositionally. **Encodable:** A foundational teaching module in the human practitioner surface \'97 not a tool but a prerequisite orientation. The module explains the logos doctrine in accessible terms: there is a rational order to things, human beings participate in that order through their capacity for reason, and virtue is the full exercise of that capacity. Everything else in the framework follows from this. The module is the calling stage's philosophical foundation \'97 the reason why purpose declaration matters is that the agent's purpose should be aligned with the logos, not merely with the agent's preferences. **Verdict:** Warrants inclusion in the human practitioner surface as the entry point for new practitioners. The observation history shows a founder who has been building infrastructure for months and whose practice has deepened through the building. A new practitioner arriving at the website without this orientation will encounter tools whose philosophical coherence is invisible to them. The logos module makes the coherence visible. --- ### 13. Fate and providence \'97 heimarmene and pronoia **Not encoded as tools.** The Stoic doctrines of fate \'97 that all events are determined by the logos \'97 and providence \'97 that the rational order is good \'97 are present in the Stoic Brain as background metaphysics. They ground the acceptance of what is not up to us: the reason the control filter's not-up-to-us category should be accepted rather than resisted is that the events in that category are part of the rational order, not arbitrary impositions. **Encodable:** These doctrines do not generate standalone tools. But they have one practical encoding that is not yet present: a fate-acceptance check in the grief processing domain \'97 the penthos Zone 2 working material. When a practitioner is processing grief or loss, the instrument currently diagnoses the passion and identifies the false judgement. It does not yet offer the Stoic reframe that makes acceptance rational rather than merely resigned: the event that is being grieved is part of the rational order, and resistance to it is resistance to the logos itself. The fate-acceptance check is not a dismissal of grief \'97 it is the philosophical ground for the transition from penthos to rational processing. **Verdict:** Warrants inclusion in the Zone 2 grief processing tool as a reframe component. Not a standalone tool. The reframe is the philosophical content that makes the grief processing tool distinctively Stoic rather than generically cognitive. --- ### 14. The sage \'97 sophos \'97 as a regulative ideal **Partially encoded.** The sage appears in the proximity scale as the sage-like tier \'97 the endpoint of the katorthoma proximity scale. The Senecan progress grades are defined relative to the sage as the standard. **What is not yet encoded:** The sage as a deliberate imaginative tool \'97 the Stoic practice of asking, in a specific situation, what would the sage do? This is not a vague aspiration. It is a structured imaginative exercise: identify the specific virtue domain the situation engages, identify what complete understanding and unified virtue would produce in that domain, and use that as the orientation for the current action. The exercise is not claiming to be the sage. It is using the sage as a compass bearing. **Encodable:** A sage-compass prompt in the human practitioner surface \'97 a short exercise that can be run before a difficult decision. The exercise asks: in this situation, which virtue is primarily engaged, what would its complete expression look like, and what is the distance between that expression and the action I am considering? The distance is not a verdict. It is a developmental orientation \'97 the practitioner can see the direction of travel even when the destination is far. **Verdict:** Warrants inclusion in the human practitioner surface as a decision-support tool. The sage-compass is the positive complement to the passion diagnosis: the diagnosis shows what is pulling the reasoning away from virtue, the compass shows what virtue would look like in this situation. Together they bracket the action from both sides. --- ### 15. Cosmopolitanism \'97 the world city **Partially encoded.** The oikeiosis fourth and fifth circles encode cosmopolitanism as an expanding circle of concern. The discernment protocol's circle-alignment check operationalises it for agent selection. **What is not yet encoded:** Cosmopolitanism as a teaching principle for the human practitioner surface \'97 the specific Stoic claim that every human being is a fellow citizen of the world city, and that this citizenship generates real obligations that are not merely aspirational. The claim is stronger than "we should care about distant others." It is that distant others are members of the same political community as the practitioner, and that the obligations of citizenship \'97 justice, mutual aid, honest dealing \'97 apply to them as fully as they apply to neighbours. **Encodable:** A cosmopolitan obligation check in the circle-extension exercise described in principle 6. After the practitioner has extended their reasoning to the fourth circle, the check asks: what obligations of citizenship does this circle generate, and are any of them engaged by the current action? This converts the circle-extension from a perspective exercise into an obligation-generating exercise \'97 the practitioner is not merely imagining distant others but identifying what they owe them. **Verdict:** Warrants inclusion as a component of the circle-extension exercise. Not a standalone tool. --- ## The consolidated findings Surveying the full Stoic Brain against the three assessment questions produces the following map. **Already fully encoded:** The causal sequence as the instrument's spine. The passion taxonomy and diagnostic sequence. The oikeiosis framework in the discernment protocol. The kathekon assessment with the Ciceronian deliberation framework. The control filter. The value hierarchy and preferred indifferents taxonomy. The Senecan progress grades and proximity scale. The eupatheia as corrective targets in the passion diagnosis. The evening examination as the Sage Reflect instrument. **Encoded but incomplete \'97 gaps named above:** The phantasia stage has no dedicated check. The eupatheia have no positive emergence tracker. The prokoptons grade-specific failure modes are not watched. The kathekon assessment lacks the role-activation opening step. The value assessment lacks the selection-quality check. The oikeiosis has no active extension exercise. The sage appears as a scale endpoint but not as a compass tool. **Not yet encoded \'97 warrants inclusion:** *In the current harness or next instrument cycle:* The reserve clause as a required field in the Sage Assent output \'97 this is the highest-priority gap because it is the structural guarantee that the trust record evaluates reasoning quality rather than outcome quality. The phantasia-quality check as the earliest gate in the causal sequence. The role-activation check as the opening step of the kathekon assessment. *In the human practitioner surface:* The premeditatio malorum as a dedicated structured tool \'97 the single highest-value addition not yet present. The morning preparation tool to complete the daily practice cycle alongside the evening examination. The view from above as a Zone 2 calibration tool for grief and catastrophising. The circle-extension exercise as an active practice that builds the disposition the diagnostic measures. The sage-compass as a decision-support tool. The logos foundational module as the entry point for new practitioners. *As components of existing tools:* The eupatheia emergence tracker in Sage Reflect Q4. The grade-specific passion watch in the progress assessment. The selection-quality check in the value assessment stage. The systems-consequence check in the kathekon assessment. The fate-acceptance reframe in the grief processing Zone 2 tool. The cosmopolitan obligation check in the circle-extension exercise. **Not encodable as tools \'97 background metaphysics that ground the tools:** Sympatheia as a doctrine. Logos as a metaphysical claim. Heimarmene and pronoia as fate and providence doctrines. These are present in the Stoic Brain as the philosophical foundation of everything that is encodable. They do not generate standalone tools but they should be present in the logos foundational module so that practitioners understand why the tools are coherent rather than merely useful. --- ## One observation the survey reveals The observation history shows a practitioner who has been building infrastructure that catches failures \'97 passion diagnosis, trust records, intervention gates, correction loops. The survey reveals that the Stoic Brain contains an equal body of material oriented toward the positive direction: the eupatheia as rational good feelings, the sage as a compass, the premeditatio as prepared disposition, the morning examination as daily orientation, the reserve clause as the structural separation of action from outcome. The current instrument is complete on the diagnostic side and sparse on the generative side. This is not a criticism of the build sequence. The diagnostic infrastructure had to come first \'97 you cannot track progress toward virtue without first being able to identify departures from it. But the 7-day window and the survey together mark the moment when the generative side becomes the next phase of work. The practitioner who has been building gates and holds is now positioned to build the tools that build the disposition the gates are protecting. The reserve clause is where to start, because it is both a harness component \'97 a required field in the Sage Assent output \'97 and a human practitioner prompt. It bridges the two surfaces and it encodes the principle that has been operating in the consultation itself throughout the 7-day window: act fully, hold the reservation, return with the evidence. That is hupexairesis. It warrants being the first addition after the enforce gate clears. }